q — equivalent continuous level over your chosen averaging window\n• LCpeak — true C-weighted peak, instant and max-hold\n• TWA — time-weighted average for noise-exposure style monitoring\n• Instant, average, and max-hold values side by side\n\nLIVE SPECTRUM\n• Real-time octave-band spectrum analyzer\n• Drag across the display to read the level at any frequency\n• Double-tap to expand for a full-screen view\n\nFLEXIBLE INPUT\n• Use the built-in microphone or any connected USB, Bluetooth, or headset input\n• Multi-channel interfaces supported — pick the exact input channel\n• A/B capture: freeze two readings and see the difference\n\nDESIGNED FOR REAL WORK\n• Choose your averaging window to suit the room and the source\n• Custom thresholds and profiles\n• Clean, high-contrast layout that reads at a glance on stage or in the field\n• Universal — optimized for both iPhone and iPad\n\nPRIVATE BY DESIGN\nSPL Meter does all processing on-device. Audio is never recorded, saved, or transmitted. There are no accounts, no analytics, no tracking, and no ads.\n\nA NOTE ON ACCURACY\nLike any phone-based meter, readings depend on your device's microphone and are not a substitute for a calibrated Class 1/2 sound level meter for compliance work. SPL Meter is a powerful, consistent tool for monitoring, comparison, and setup — not a certified measurement instrument.", "trackCensoredName": "ARCQ SPL - SPL Meter", "trackViewUrl": "https://apps.apple.com/kr/app/arcq-spl-spl-meter/id6782095826?uo=4", "contentAdvisoryRating": "4+", "averageUserRating": 4.875, "genres": ["유틸리티", "음악"], "userRatingCount": 8}]}